# Styx @VERSION@ — Linux Gateway

For a Linux server that connects your computers to ChatGPT. This package runs the
Gateway only; it does not run commands, browsers or Computer Use on this server.

Extract the archive, enter its folder, and start installation:

```sh
cd @BUNDLE@
./install.sh
```

The installer keeps Styx in your user data directory, registers the `styx`
command, and opens setup. No administrator shell is needed. After installation
you can remove the extracted folder; the installed program is retained separately.

Setup runs the Gateway as your systemd user service. To keep it running after you
log out, systemd linger must be enabled for your account. The installer explains
when system authorization is needed; this package does not run a sudo script or
silently change that setting.

You can invite computers before connecting ChatGPT, then configure the Gateway's
Tunnel later. Connected computers use this one Gateway connection.

Use `styx quit` to stop Styx and `styx start` to start it again. To remove its
user services while retaining your configuration, run `styx uninstall`.
Install a newer package through its same `./install.sh` entry; the installer
updates an existing setup and preserves its configuration.
